      "rationale": "🐍️ No third-party library reads or writes process.process3d's .dsl.semio carrier — G-code parsers and STEP/BREP kernels were surveyed and DECLINED (kept verbatim below in this history). The reference is therefore a SECOND IMPLEMENTATION rather than a third-party distribution. The implementation is ../../../🧪️tests/🌷️mutate-process3d-1/🐍️.py, written from this subset's own committed ../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/🔣️.json and each mutation's 🧬️.schema.json, and from .🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️08/☀️12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-DIRECT-LEAF-OVERHAUL/📓️taxonomy.md's create/delete/rename/change/replace/move/reorder verb entries and 📓️derivation-rules.md's per-shape recipes. It imports nothing from the Rust it judges and transliterates none of it. Honest boundary: steps is a content-addressed child handle minting a new childId (and toolSolids entries mint their own) on every stepPayloads change, through a digest algorithm no schema in this repository publishes, so the seven step-scoped kinds verify stepPayloads itself (the real content) rather than claiming to reproduce that hash; the other nine kinds touch no content-addressed field (replace-stock-solid's new handle is supplied verbatim by the payload, not computed) and are verified as a full snapshot equality. A first standalone run caught a real bug (change-step-origin's inverse assumed the optional origin key was always present) fixed before registration. All sixteen kinds' forward and inverse scenarios were executed standalone via the repository's own 🧰️framework/🛍️products/🦑️repo/🔨️modules/🧪️test/📦️packages/🐍️python/🐍️.py host against a hand-built plan — all thirty-two passed after the fix.",
